KG42.register("rules-7340deed3d701e6847d81e7b",{"id":"19-two_stage_battery_sharing::v141-c-R004","paper":"19-two_stage_battery_sharing","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R004","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Prosumer participation","process_stage":"participation","market_meaning":"Prosumers may participate in neighborhood P2P energy sharing through local buying and selling. Scope: Prosumer participation in neighborhood P2P energy sharing within a community Microgrid.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function participation.prosumer under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["participation.prosumer"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"participation","context_text":"Prosumer participation in neighborhood P2P energy sharing within a community Microgrid.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e007"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Prosumers may participate in neighborhood P2P energy sharing through local buying and selling. Scope: Prosumer participation in neighborhood P2P energy sharing within a community Microgrid.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["participation.prosumer"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e007"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e007","location":{"location_id":"src-b91cee592e-p04-c1r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":4,"printed_page":"264","section":"2.1. P2P energy sharing structure","anchor_text":"g p g time when there is insuﬃcient energy from the PV battery system, the prosumer buys energy from","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 1","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"P2P energy sharing provides options for prosumers to trade energy within the neighborhood through local buying and selling, allowing local funds to remain within the local economy [31]. With P2P energy sharing, several customers in a community Microgrid share the connection to the main grid. The combined load is subject to random coincidence of the individual loads, which averages stochastic fluctuations [32,33]. This means that surplus PV power from a customer can be consumed by another customer with excess consumption.\nFig. 1 shows the architecture of P2P energy sharing. In the P2P sharing community, there are N customers, NB of which have individual PV battery systems installed (NB ⩽ N). Although the PV outputs in a community are likely to be similar due to almost the same solar radiation, the net loads vary between prosumers, because of the differences in load, kWp of PV systems and battery statuses. Therefore, it is possible for the prosumers to share PV power with each other. The surplus PV power from prosumers can also be traded with consumers who do not have PV systems."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":"The source states a qualitative participation permission/scope for prosumers ('provides options ... through local buying and selling') and does not define a design-selection or operational decision variable for this rule. The N/NB counts in the same passage are participant-population counts, not decision variables.","empty_theta_reason":"No fixed parameter is defined for this participation permission in the frozen graph. The passage mentions N and NB, but they characterize community composition and the frozen graph has only participation.prosumer, so treating them as parameters would require representing total-customer scope not present in this rule."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-participation"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"participation.prosumer","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e007","quote":"P2P energy sharing provides options for prosumers to trade energy within the neighborhood through local buying and selling, allowing local funds to remain within the local economy [31]."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"e2ad0fab0deb4c172a8a9bb1e59c1e637aa25ec6dfb9623169e598d450f294a9","applicability":"non_mathematical","reason":"The source-supported content for this rule is a qualitative participation permission and scope: P2P energy sharing provides options for prosumers to trade energy within the neighborhood through local buying and selling. The passage does not define a design-selection or operational decision variable, a parameterized participation condition, or an objective/constraint expression for this permission. The N/NB counts in the same passage describe community composition, not a decision rule, and the frozen graph contains only participation.prosumer. B evidence remains unreviewed; no source expression is asserted.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R004-C001","node_ids":["participation.prosumer"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The rule's sole frozen node is participation.prosumer. The constraint is a procedural permission scoped to that participation role; the frozen graph contains no edge to bind. The source quote supports the prosumer local buying-and-selling scope."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
